  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Ministry of Labor&#x2019;s capacity to design interventions and manage for results</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the IDF grant is to strengthen the capacity of the newly established Ministry of Labor to fulfill its mandate using strong country systems that focus on performance and results. This will be achieved through the development of the tools required to design, implement, and monitor labor market policies that are informed by information and evidence; and that focus on results and performance.  The IDF grant would finance 3 components: (1)   Component 1: Setting up a system for labor market monitoring and analysis, that will inform policy development and guide evidence-based resource allocation. [$175,000] (2)   Component 2: Designing the National Employment Service and developing the tools for performance-based contracting of its services. [$325,000] (3)   Component 3: Developing the systems of the Temporary Employment Program. [$225,000]</narrative>
  </description>
